1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,600
Hello?

2
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,786
Hi.

3
00:00:01,786 --> 00:00:02,348
It's Laura Carlton here.

4
00:00:02,348 --> 00:00:04,795
We've just arrived at the holiday flat,

5
00:00:04,795 --> 00:00:08,640
but I can't get the hot water and heating to work.

6
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:09,977
Oh right!

7
00:00:09,977 --> 00:00:11,313
That's easy.

8
00:00:11,313 --> 00:00:12,650
Don't worry.

9
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:15,780
In the upstairs cupboard, you'll find the water heater.

10
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:20,110
You'll see three main controls on the left at the bottom of the heater.

11
00:00:20,110 --> 00:00:26,064
The first one-the round one on the far left-is the most important one for the heating

12
00:00:26,064 --> 00:00:27,180
and hot water.

13
00:00:27,180 --> 00:00:28,980
It's the main control switch.

14
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:31,500
Make sure it's in the 'on' position.

15
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:33,436
The switch itself doesn't light up,

16
00:00:33,436 --> 00:00:37,630
but the little square below will be black if the switch is 'off'.

17
00:00:37,630 --> 00:00:41,820
That's probably what's happened-it's got switched off by mistake.

18
00:00:41,820 --> 00:00:47,733
The middle one of these three controls-you'll see it's slightly larger than the first

19
00:00:47,733 --> 00:00:49,000
one-controls the radiators.

20
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,598
If you feel cold while you're there and need the radiators on, this needs

21
00:00:53,598 --> 00:00:55,240
to be turned to maximum.

22
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:59,807
The last of the three controls-the one on the right-is usually on about a

23
00:00:59,807 --> 00:01:04,374
number for setting which for the water in the taps is usually quite hot

24
00:01:04,374 --> 00:01:04,700
enough.

25
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:10,440
Below the heating controls in the middle is a small round plastic button.

26
00:01:10,440 --> 00:01:14,950
If there isn't enough water in the pipes, sometimes the heater goes out.

27
00:01:14,950 --> 00:01:19,070
If this happens you'll need to press this button to reset the heater.

28
00:01:19,070 --> 00:01:24,280
Hold it in for about five seconds and the heater should come on again.

29
00:01:24,280 --> 00:01:29,495
Then there's a little square indicator under the third knob that's a kind of

30
00:01:29,495 --> 00:01:30,240
alarm light.

31
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:32,800
It'll flash if you need to reset the heater.

32
00:01:32,800 --> 00:01:35,440
It sounds complicated…

33
00:01:35,440 --> 00:01:38,500
I'm sure you won't have any problems with it.

34
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:42,310
There should be some more instructions on the side of the heater.

35
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:44,700
Call me back if you can't make it work.

36
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:47,330
Okay.

37
00:01:47,330 --> 00:01:52,288
While you're on the phone, we haven't managed to find a few things we

38
00:01:52,288 --> 00:01:56,183
need, like extra pillows for the beds and some washing powder.

39
00:01:56,183 --> 00:01:57,600
Is there any here?

40
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:58,500
Pillows… yes.

41
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:04,800
If you look in the cupboard, the large white one upstairs-to the left of

42
00:02:04,800 --> 00:02:10,200
the bathroom door-there should be four or five on the top shelf.

43
00:02:10,200 --> 00:02:17,083
And if you want to do some washing, there's some powder for that…probably by

44
00:02:17,083 --> 00:02:18,460
the back door.

45
00:02:18,460 --> 00:02:21,380
There's a kind of shelf there above the sink.

46
00:02:21,380 --> 00:02:25,264
In fact, I'm sure there's some there, in a large blue box.

47
00:02:25,264 --> 00:02:28,500
You need about half a cup full for each wash.

48
00:02:28,500 --> 00:02:33,167
And that reminds me, the spare key to the back door is hanging on

49
00:02:33,167 --> 00:02:36,500
a hook on the wall by the sitting room window.

50
00:02:36,500 --> 00:02:39,850
Please make sure to put it back when you've used it.

51
00:02:39,850 --> 00:02:43,376
The previous guests lost it in the garden and I had to get another

52
00:02:43,376 --> 00:02:43,880
one made!

53
00:02:43,880 --> 00:02:48,529
And if you have any trouble with the lamps, you'll find some spare bulbs

54
00:02:48,529 --> 00:02:50,190
in a large cardboard box.

55
00:02:50,190 --> 00:02:54,250
It's on top of the washing machine with all kinds of useful things in

56
00:02:54,250 --> 00:02:54,540
it.

57
00:02:54,540 --> 00:02:54,888
Oh,

58
00:02:54,888 --> 00:02:58,710
and another thing I forgot to mention when we last spoke…

59
00:02:58,710 --> 00:02:59,460
Yes?

60
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:01,136
I've left you a local map,

61
00:03:01,136 --> 00:03:03,930
so you'll be able to find your way around easily.

62
00:03:03,930 --> 00:03:05,520
It shows the whole area.

63
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:09,974
I put it in the top drawer of the chest under the TV in

64
00:03:09,974 --> 00:03:10,610
your bedroom.

65
00:03:10,610 --> 00:03:13,850
There's a whole file of local information in there too.

66
00:03:13,850 --> 00:03:14,253
Thanks.

67
00:03:14,253 --> 00:03:16,270
What about visiting the town?

68
00:03:16,270 --> 00:03:18,690
Can you give us any advice?

69
00:03:18,690 --> 00:03:19,176
Yes.

70
00:03:19,176 --> 00:03:22,090
You'll need to take the car.

71
00:03:22,090 --> 00:03:24,660
It's too far to talk from the flat really.

72
00:03:24,660 --> 00:03:28,352
You have to pay to leave your car in all the car parks now

73
00:03:28,352 --> 00:03:31,252
I'm afraid…I like the one that's by the station best

74
00:03:31,252 --> 00:03:34,680
and you can walk to the town centre from there in five minutes.

75
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:37,000
That's where all the best restaurants are.

76
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:41,515
But if you want a takeaway, the ltalian one does really good pasta

77
00:03:41,515 --> 00:03:42,210
and pizzas.

78
00:03:42,210 --> 00:03:46,019
Call 7-3 double 2,8-1for that one,

79
00:03:46,019 --> 00:03:51,460
or 7 double 6, double 1, 9 for the Chinese.

80
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:54,890
They're both good and they'll both deliver to the flat.

81
00:03:54,890 --> 00:04:01,180
As for places to visit, yes, do go and see the railway museum.

82
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:04,220
The exhibition is small but really good.

83
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:06,374
It gets very crowded on Sundays,

84
00:04:06,374 --> 00:04:11,399
so I suggest you visit it on a quieter day, later in the week,

85
00:04:11,399 --> 00:04:16,066
but not on Thursdays which is market day-you won't find anywhere to park

86
00:04:16,066 --> 00:04:20,732
and it's also the only day of the week when they're not open!

87
00:04:20,732 --> 00:04:21,450
Anything else?

88
00:04:21,450 --> 00:04:23,290
Not for the moment.

89
00:04:23,290 --> 00:04:23,750
Thanks!
